Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Policy Not Propagating to Managed Clusters
Symptoms: Policy shows as created but not appearing on managed clusters

Solution:

# Check placement rule and binding
oc get placementrule -n policies
oc get placementbinding -n policies

# Verify cluster labels match placement rule selectors
oc get managedclusters --show-labels

# Check policy controller logs
oc logs -n open-cluster-management deployment/governance-policy-propagator
Issue 2: Policy Violations Not Being Detected
Symptoms: Non-compliant resources exist but policy shows compliant

Solution:

# Check configuration policy status
oc describe configurationpolicy -A

# Verify namespace selectors
oc get policy <policy-name> -n policies -o yaml | grep -A 5 namespaceSelector

# Check policy evaluation frequency
oc get configurationpolicy -A -o jsonpath='{.items[*].spec.evaluationInterval}'
Issue 3: Remediation Not Working
Symptoms: Policy detects violations but doesn't fix them

Solution:

# Verify remediation action is set to enforce
oc get policy <policy-name> -n policies -o jsonpath='{.spec.remediationAction}'

